52. Final controlling rule

The agent determines meaning where meaning cannot be reduced mechanically.

The application determines:
- raw-input custody;
- identity;
- raw input enumeration;
- current input selection;
- coverage that is mechanically observable;
- admissibility;
- execution routing;
- deterministic computation;
- byte identity;
- current scope;
- independence where observable;
- evidence sufficiency where objectively knowable;
- contradiction sets;
- stability;
- lifecycle state;
- every deterministic gate;
- release.

Stage 01 is the first semantic intake stage.
No implementation may assume that the application already extracted arbitrary user-file meaning before the Stage 01 agent inspected the file.
After Stage 01 accepts the extracted human-authority information, no later stage may ask the user to supply that information again.
Stage 04 must receive the complete current Stage 01 human-origin information and complete current Stage 03 research automatically.
No human or agent assertion may substitute for a fact the application can establish itself.
No test, audit, source review, or deployment result substitutes for using the live application through the exact visible path.

The implementation is complete only when all boundaries exist in code, are visible in the operator experience, survive reload and failure, preserve the approved visuals, pass the complete regression suite, function through all 30 stages, and are verified against the exact deployed bytes.

The controlling specification text itself is implementation authority, not application project content. The application MUST implement the contract; it MUST NOT carry, display, transmit, or treat this specification text as runtime canonical state merely to establish what contract applies.

The controlling external exchange is file-first. prompt-engine.js creates the exact authoritative prompt-file bytes; the application exports those bytes and the manifest-selected files; the application ingests the exact response JSON file and attachment-slot files. Clipboard and pasted text are never required canonical transports.

Implementation-only instructions, repository audits, specification text, and repository governance manifests are not runtime project content and are not delegated to external stage agents.

Every release-bearing semantic value uses the independent-review contract where required. Every obligation is evaluated only when due. Every application-owned calculation commits through its validated direct command rather than artificial human proposal approval.

Final delivery uses the exact Stage 25 delivery-candidate set, Stage 27 release precedence, Stage 28 byte identity and destination-bound human intent, Stage 29 evidence-chain hash, pre-delivery checkpoint, and the atomic Stage 30 terminal command. Authorization, delivery attempt, and completed delivery are distinct.

Completion additionally requires the current exact deployed origin and bytes and the pinned actual physical-iPhone Safari operator path.

